  "table1": {
    "caption": "Table 1 Composition of the analysis set, with the sequencing study, administrative region and collection period that accompany each agro-ecological zone. Zone is very nearly a relabelling of region and study: three of the four zones draw on a single administrative region, and one on a single study. The final column is measured on the pre-filter quality-control cohort of 4,905 isolates, not on the analysis set: every analysed isolate satisfies Fws ≥ 0.95 by construction, so its polyclonal fraction is zero. QC-cohort denominators are given in the column.",
    "following_paragraph": "Zone sizes are strongly unequal. Guinea savanna contributes 1,334 isolates, deciduous forest 337, coastal savanna 204 and the transitional zone 25. Zone is also very nearly a relabelling of administrative region, sequencing study and collection period: three of the four zones are dominated by a single study, and Guinea savanna, which here is effectively Upper East region, supplies 1,334 of 1,900 isolates (70.2%). Seven administrative regions are the finest spatial unit available in the release metadata. Because study membership varies together with collection year, finer geography, recruitment and host biology, holding zone constant does not isolate a technical cause; the comparisons below can demonstrate study-associated heterogeneity but not a sequencing artefact.",
